  "english": "22. Saturday. Tone 2 [BK]. The Holy Patriarchs Basil and the others.\n23. Sunday. Tone 7 [GZCh]. Fifth [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Who from eternity\" (Nakhayavedyan). Dismissal Hymn Tone 5 [GDz]: \"By the sign of the cross\" (I khachanish), to the end.\n24. Monday. Tone 6 [GK]. David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n29. Saturday. Tone 3 [BZ]. The Sons of Thunder. Eve of the Nativity Fast.\n30. Sunday. Tone 2 [BK]. Sixth [Sunday]. Fast. Dismissal Hymn Tone 2 [B]: \"They anticipated\" (Kankhetsin), to the end.\n31. Monday. Tone 4 [GZ]. Fast. Father [Hymn] Tone 8 [DK]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord, the God of our fathers\". And see the rest according to the order.\n\nJanuary:\n5. Saturday. Tone 1 [AK]. Eve [Jrakaluyts] of the Nativity of Christ.\n\n2. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Second [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 2 [BK]: \"Unoriginate God\" (Ansgizpn astuats). Dismissal Hymn Tone 8 [DK]: \"Thine angel, O Lord\" (Hreshtak ko ter).\n3. Monday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Bishop Genarios, and the soldier Mercourius, and Jacob and Iravapar.\n4. Wednesday. Tone 1 [AK]. King Abgar. The Scripture readings and Gospel are those of Theodosius.\n9. Sunday. Tone 7 [DZ]. Third [Sunday]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n12. Wednesday. Tone 1 [AK]. Father [Hymn] of Fasting Tone 7 [D3]: \"Who for the three youths\".\n16. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 5 [G3]: \"Glorified Son\". Dismissal Hymn Tone 6 [GK]: \"Assumed and our\".\n\nThe Romenic Weekly Cycle: 7.\nJanuary:\n6. FRIDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The fasting-free period [midjots outik] is thirty-one days.\n14. Saturday. John the Forerunner [Karapet].\n15. Sunday. First [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 5 [GDz]: \"The dawning of the Only-begotten\".\n16. Monday. Patriarch Peter, Blaise, and the others.\n17. Tuesday. Anthony, and Tryphon, Parsamas, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n19. Thursday. King Theodosius, and the Holy Infants of Ephesus.\n21. Saturday. The Patriarchs Athanasius and Cyril.\n22. Sunday. Second [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 5 [G3]: \"Creator of creatures\".\n23. Monday. Cyriacus and Julitta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris.\n24. Tuesday. Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugenie the virgin, and the others.\n26. Thursday. Eugene, Macarius, and the others.\n28. Saturday. Gregory the Theologian.\n29. Sunday. Third [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Today he is sacrificed\". Refer to the one-week section placed below in the First Volume, where you will look for Transfiguration [Vartavar].\n30. Monday. The Maccabees: Eleazar and the others.\n31. Tuesday. The Twelve Prophets: Hosea and the others.\n\nFebruary:\n2. Thursday. Sophia and her three daughters.\n4. Saturday. The Sons and Grandsons of the Enlightener.",
